{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>For the yoke of his burden.</b> The noun patterns vary." "<b>Rod.</b> That strikes his shoulder." "<b>החתות.</b> The he is opened [pathach] because of a guttural letter, like החלות (Deuteronomy 3:24), and it is not a foreign word, and the tav of החתות faces [the object, i.e. is in the objective case], like הרבית הגוי." "<b>As the day of Midian.</b> In the days of Gideon (Judges 7[:22])."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {2 "Ibn Ezra's grammatical terminology: פתוח = pathach vowel; אות הגרון = guttural consonant; לנוכח = objective case marker.", 3 "The verse citation in the source reads Judges 7:21–22; Ibn Ezra likely intends the battle's culmination in v. 22."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:58.436661481Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}